# Licence for the station dataset

`stations.json` is **not** covered by the MIT licence in the repository root. That
licence covers the code. This file covers the data.

## What it is licensed under

Station identity, operator, status, transmission schedules, frequency lists and most of
the station descriptions in `stations.json` are adapted from
[Priyom.org](https://priyom.org/), which publishes its
material under the **Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
International** licence:

<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/>

`stations.json`, and any build that embeds it, is distributed under that same licence.
Three obligations follow, and they are obligations rather than courtesies:

- **Attribution.** Priyom.org is credited on every station page in the app, in the help
  screen, and here. The ENIGMA 2000 control list at <http://www.signalshed.com/> is
  credited the same way for the designator assignments it originates.
- **NonCommercial.** This project takes no money — no advertising, no paid tier, no
  donations. See [docs/PLAN.md](../docs/PLAN.md) §7, where a donation page was
  considered and dropped.
- **ShareAlike.** Anyone redistributing this dataset, or a dataset adapted from it, must
  do so under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

## What was changed

The licence requires that adaptations say so. The data here has been:

- reformatted from HTML tables into JSON;
- restructured so each schedule slot carries twelve monthly frequencies, expanded from
  the merged month columns Priyom renders with `colspan`;
- encoded as RFC 5545 `RRULE` strings rather than day-and-time text;
- filtered — rows Priyom marks as outdated by rendering them in italics are omitted, as
  are slots with no published frequency in any month;
- merged with material from the ENIGMA 2000 control list and, for a few stations,
  Wikipedia and numbers-stations.com, each carrying its own `sourceUrl`.

Station descriptions are **quoted, not adapted**. Each one is a verbatim extract of the
prose on a Priyom station page, held in `lore.text` with the page in `lore.quotedFrom`,
and rendered in the app as a quotation with that link and this licence beside it. Two
things were removed: paragraphs that referred to something laid out on the page, which
say nothing once the words are elsewhere, and everything in a table. Twelve descriptions
were written for this archive rather than quoted, and carry `lore.quotedFrom: null`.

Nothing was invented. `scripts/import-priyom.mjs` and `scripts/import-lore.mjs` perform
the transformation and can be re-run to reproduce it.

No message content is reproduced. Priyom publishes logs of received transmissions and
lays each station's message formats out as tables of sample five-figure groups; both
importers refuse to read tables, for the reason in
[docs/RESEARCH.md](../docs/RESEARCH.md) §5.

## The live markers

The Buzzer, The Pip and The Squeaky Wheel entries carry frequencies sourced from
Wikipedia and numbers-stations.com rather than from Priyom, each cited in the row's own
`sourceUrl`. They are hand-written, not imported.
